 "verdict": "Not numerical non-determinism and not a recording gap. At this state every serving and environment check reproduced. The prompt at h_t is equal. a_d2 replays bit-exactly on its own server and is identical across the two tasks (GPU 2 vs GPU 7). The tool output, the final DB hash, the budget and every outcome field equal the original and the reference. In the same tasks the BB no-ops (15/15) and the QQ re-runs (18/18) are byte-exact. The q4 BF16 TP=1 path is inside the verified 257/257 envelope at running <= 8 and waiting 0. The failure is a comparison artifact of the implicit-identity precondition. The d2 checkpoint deterministically emits the four keys of arguments.flights[0] in a different order. BF16's logit margin at that token is 0.25, the smallest of the decision, so this is a near-tie flipped by the d2 weights. canon_msg treats the reordered dict as equal, but the chat template renders insertion order, so the continuation conditions on a different prompt, 24 tokens permuted, and produces different text. The protocol states the precondition as canonical equality (§2 'Implicit identity'), so both checks applied and failed on suffix and prompt identity. §4 'Block quarantine' removes the block on any failed implicit identity. The quarantine of f01 was correctly triggered under the frozen rule.",
